"The Software" means everything in this repository (code, documentation, examples, the skill, images
and video), except the Inter font in fonts/ and the sound effects in sfx/. "Your videos" means the videos, images,
audio and other media you make by running the Software.

The Software is source available, not open source. You may read it and use it to make your own videos.
You may not copy it, change it, share it, sell it or rebuild it.

1. What you may do

   a. Read and study the Software.
   b. Download, install and run the Software, unmodified, on computers you own or control, to make
      your videos. This includes installing the skill in skills/ and running the MCP server in mcp/
      (directly or as the Claude Code plugin) for an AI agent that you direct.
   c. Write your own scene files that call the Software, and use the example scenes in examples/ as a
      starting point for them. Scene files you write are yours.
   d. Use, publish and sell your videos, for personal or commercial work, including work for your own
      clients, with no fee. You own your videos. Credit ("Made with idra-motion") is welcome but not
      required.

2. What you may not do

   a. Except as section 1 allows, copy, share, publish, distribute, sublicense, sell, rent or lend the
      Software or any substantial part of it, in source or any other form.
   b. Modify the Software, or make, share or publish modified versions of it or works based on it. You
      may make small private changes needed to run it on your own computers, as long as you never share
      them. Your own scene files are not affected by this.
   c. Offer the Software, or anything built with its code, to others as a product or service: for
      example a hosted renderer, an API, an app, a template pack or a video generation tool. Making
      videos for your own clients is allowed (section 1d).
   d. Recreate the Software: use its code, documentation or skill to build, or to help anyone build, a
      tool, library, service or skill that does the same job as the Software or competes with it.
   e. Use the Software, its documentation or its skill to train or fine-tune a machine learning model,
      or put them in a dataset.
   f. Remove or change this licence, the copyright notices or CREDITS.md.
   g. Use the names IDRA or idra-motion, or the IDRA logo, to name or promote your own product. You may
      say that a video was made with idra-motion.

